WEBVTT

00:36:28.231 --> 00:36:30.601
You will pass where
my grandfather had a law firm.

00:36:30.625 --> 00:36:33.188
You will pass where my mother
and father both grew up,

00:36:33.212 --> 00:36:36.381
where I grew up and, right now,
where my son is in college.

00:36:36.405 --> 00:36:38.192
So that's five generations.

00:36:38.216 --> 00:36:41.717
And when you go back
and look through this neighborhood ...

00:36:41.741 --> 00:36:44.816
When my grandfather, once, he wrote me
a map of the neighborhood,

00:36:44.840 --> 00:36:45.997
Lower Manhattan.

00:36:46.021 --> 00:36:48.957
And there were Finnish buildings,
there were German buildings,

00:36:48.981 --> 00:36:51.820
there were Bohemian buildings,
there were Russian buildings.

00:36:51.844 --> 00:36:54.959
This all seemed incredibly polyglot
and multicultural at the time.

00:36:54.983 --> 00:36:57.989
And it had tensions -- I mean,
if you walked by a wrong building

00:36:58.013 --> 00:36:59.164
the wrong day,

00:36:59.188 --> 00:37:00.625
kids would throw rocks at you.